    "title": "Maryville couple charged with child abuse - NewsBreak",
    "text": "A Maryville couple has been charged with child abuse/neglect after Blount County Sheriff's deputies found that the family, which included a 4-year-old child, was living in what a BCSO press release described as \"squalid\" conditions. Allen Michael Westmoreland, 29, and Sandra Jean Gridley, 27, were both charged after deputies responded to a call that dogs were tied up behind their Calderwood Highway home without access to food, water or shelter. The release said that when deputies arrived, they discovered three dogs that appeared emaciated, chained up behind the house. During the investigation, deputies and investigators discovered the home was \"rife with bugs\" and that animal feces were found throughout the home. Deputies also said the house had no electricity and minimal running water. According to the release, the child was placed into the custody of the Department of Children's Services, and four dogs were placed into the care of Blount County Animal Center. Westmoreland and Gridley were arrested around 5:45 p.m. Tuesday and are being held in lieu of bonds totaling $7,500 each pending 1:30 p.m. Aug. 6 hearings in Blount County General Sessions Court. Subscribe to The Daily Times",
